# Processed Dataset Notice & Reproduction Guide

Due to GitHub's file storage limitations, the preprocessed feature matrices and split arrays in `dataset/pre_data/` are **not included** in this repository.

You can easily generate all processed data files locally with a single script:

### Step 1. Ensure Raw Data is Downloaded
Make sure you have downloaded the raw single-cell multi-omics datasets and placed them into the `data/` directory according to the file list provided in **Supplementary Table S2**. The directory structure should match:

├── data/                                 # Raw multi-omics datasets (downloaded separately according to the file list in Table S2 in supplementary)
│   ├── PBMC_10k/                         # 10x Multiome PBMC
│   ├── BMMC/                             # NeurIPS 2021 Multiome BMMC
│   ├── Human_Fetal_Brain/                # Chunked TSV multi-files
│   ├── MouseKidney_sciCAR/               # sci-CAR triplet format
│   ├── SHARE_seq_Brain/                  # SHARE-seq raw files
│   ├── SHARE_seq_SkinA/                  # Dual h5ad format
│   ├── SHARE_seq_SkinB/                  # Large-scale streaming files
│   ├── SNARE_seq_AdBC/                   # Adult brain cortex MTX triplets
│   ├── SNARE_seq_Cortex/                 # Dual h5ad format
│   └── SNARE_seq_P0BC/                   # P0 brain cortex MTX triplets

### Step 2. Run the Preprocessing Script
python src/DataPreprocessing/preprocess_all_datasets.py

What this script will automatically generate:
  Top 2,000 highly variable genes (HVG) normalized expression matrices (RNA_matrix.npy).
  GTF-aligned promoter-activity matrices from scATAC-seq (ATAC_gene_activity.npy).
  Synchronized cell-type labels and mappings (Labels.npy, label_map.npy, gene_names.csv).
  Synchronized 5-fold cross-validation split folders (fold_1/ ~ fold_5/) with cross-model compatible formats (*.npy, *.npz, *.txt).
  Inter-donor subsets for BMMC (Source_Train_15078/ and Target_Test_19593/).

Once executed, the complete dataset/pre_data/ folder structure will be generated and ready for model training and benchmarking.
